messages:
erin: Heads-up — I'm starting a small spike to pull the inference routing 'safety hatch' out of the hotpath. Need to land interface contracts and a clear rollback playbook before we start slicing runtime. TL;DR: propose a thin compatibility shim so old router and new router variants can coexist for gradual cutover.

mike: +1 for shim approach. Question: who owns the prefix/KV cache during the transition? Router or model-host? That affects latency and state-migration cost.

sophie: Strong preference for model-host owning the KV cache. Locality wins for tail latency — router as orchestrator only.

erin: Agreed locality is good but migration complexity rises. Proposed middle-ground: define a minimal 'safety_hatch' interface that hides ownership behind two ops endpoints so either side can implement without breaking callers. Example contract sketch:
```json
{
  "probe": {
    "path": "/safety_hatch/probe",
    "method": "GET",
    "response": {"version": "string", "ready": "boolean", "kv_owner": "string"}
  },
  "rewind": {
    "path": "/safety_hatch/rewind",
    "method": "POST",
    "body": {"reason": "string", "grace_seconds": "integer"},
    "response": {"status": "ok|failed", "leased_keys": "integer"}
  }
}
```
This keeps router->service interactions stable while letting us iterate on who actually stores the cache.

ryan: CI side: we need schema-driven contract tests so the router's gating tests can assert exact probe shape and allowed fields. Suggest adding a contract test harness in the integration suite.

mike: Also need a canary rollout checklist: 1) deploy shim to staging, 2) enable probe gating in router locally, 3) shift 1% traffic -> shim, 4) monitor tail latency, token-cost delta, error-rate, 5) escalate to 10/25/100% with 15m observation windows, 6) keep rewind enabled and exercised at each step.

deploy-bot: :package: deploy-bot: Canary deployment started: safety-hatch-shim v0.1 -> staging (build 8762) :rocket:

sophie: Observability: please add route-level tracing tags (safety_hatch_v) and a token-cost-delta metric per route. If we don't surface cost/latency deltas we won't know if migration is regressing economics.

erin: Cool — I'll draft an RFC follow-up with: goals, contract schema (above), CI contract-test checklist, canary rollout steps, and a rollback playbook (exercise rewind + verify leased_keys drain). @mike @sophie @ryan can you drop constraints or missing checks by EOD? :thinking_face:
